{
  "abstract": "In the shifted Antihydra recurrence on natural-number pairs, each successful round sends x to floor(3x/2). Even x earns two units of credit. Odd x spends one unit and halts at zero credit. From (8, 0), no semilinear set containing the seed admits a successful successor within the set for every member. The proof also gives a quantitative horizontal-ray bound and the Presburger-definable corollary. The seed's halting behavior is open in this work, and priority is unclaimed.",
